SUMMARY:Quantitative Metastability in the Linear Becker-Döring Equations
DESCRIPTION:The Becker-Döring equations describe the dynamics of cluster formation and have long been known to exhibit metastable behaviour near the critical monomer concentration. In the linear setting\, where the monomer concentration is fixed\, Penrose [3\, 2] and Kreer [1] established fundamental results on the metastable regime and the long-time behaviour of solutions. In this talk\, we revisit this metastab\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16862/
